### 2. Tasks

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT6**: Open Door for Delivery | Robot opens the inpatient room door. | AND | Room door | 1 | One robot is sufficient to open the door. |
| **AT7**: Deliver Food to Table | Robot places food on the patient’s table using a special manipulation skill. | AND | Inpatient room table | 1 | Only one robot is needed for manipulation. |
| **AT8**: Deliver Food to Tray | Robot places food on its tray for patient retrieval. | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | One robot can place food on the tray. |
| **AT9**: Query Patient Retrieval Ability | Robot queries the patient record for ability to retrieve meal from the tray. | AND | Hospital database | 1 | Robot must access the record. |
| **AT10**: Indicate Meal | Robot informs the patient which meal to retrieve. | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Robot must communicate the correct meal. |
| **AT11**: Track Meal Retrieval | Robot logs the time and location of meal retrieval. | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Tracking is needed for accountability. |
| **AT12**: Alert Wrong Meal Retrieved | Robot alerts a nurse if the wrong meal is retrieved. | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Ensures error correction. |
| **AT13**: Unassisted Dish Retrieval | Robot picks up dirty dishes alone. | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Robot can handle light dish loads. |
| **AT14**: Robot‑Robot Dish Retrieval | Two robots cooperate to retrieve dishes. | AND | Inpatient room | [2,2] | Heavy loads require two robots. |
| **AT15**: Robot‑Human Dish Retrieval | Robot cooperates with a human to retrieve dishes. | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Human assistance is required. |
| **AT16**: Open Door for Dish Retrieval | Robot opens the inpatient room door for dish retrieval. | AND | Room door | 1 | Needed before dish‑retrieval actions. |

